{
  "id": "2026-10-04-ui-audit",
  "scope": "ui",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-10-04",
  "question": "What is the smallest copied composition contract that keeps kit membership, installation metadata and toolbar policy explicit?",
  "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v3",
  "trigger": "The owner asked for a best-api-review audit of every open ledger unit, judged afresh because earlier verdicts came from a weaker model, then widened it on 2026-10-04 to every existing ledger item. It asked for verdicts only, so no plan, build or panel follows in this run. This scope was closed, with a latest pursue verdict, at queue position 18. It is not the unit next returned, which was reads.",
  "requirements": [
    "Copied source installs completely for the requested provider and style, and a missing registry edge fails closed.",
    "Required package and registry-item dependencies are derived from each copied item source graph, and authored metadata holds only intent the source cannot express, such as bundles, targets, styles, CSS, optional peers and provider selection (docs/vision/plate.md:938).",
    "App and registry source own kit membership and product composition; copied provider adapters own menu focus lifecycles.",
    "Typed plugin insert and upsert own semantic block insertion; there is no universal command catalog.",
    "Registry integration behavior stays with the item it modifies, even when that needs an optional package dependency (docs/vision/plate.md:930)."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reused the 2026-09-17 and 2026-09-18 ui records, the slash-ui-actions execution receipt and the 2026-09-18 install design. Rechecked on the live tree that no transforms.ts exists under the registry, item finalFocus in both dropdown adapters and their callers, typed insert and upsert in blockInsertion.ts and the feature plugins, the remaining content-level onFinalFocus callers, and registry-package-dependencies.mts. Counted authored versus import-required registry edges with a scratch script over registry-metadata.json and the copied sources.",
  "summary": "The job is to install working copied source while kit membership, install intent and toolbar policy stay explicit. The 2026-09-18 Pursue landed. Registry transforms.ts is gone, Base and Radix dropdown items carry item-scoped finalFocus, and feature plugins own typed insert and upsert through one private blockInsertion policy. One installation-metadata gap remains. registry-package-dependencies.mts derives package dependencies, but for registry items it resolves each copied import's unique owner and then throws unless the author already listed that same edge, so registryDependencies mix import facts with install intent. A scratch census of the base registry finds that about 361 of 437 authored @plate edges are exactly what source imports require, and deriving them leaves about 76 intentional style, bundle and companion edges. Validation-only loses, because the authored edge carries nothing the checker lacks and an edge whose import was removed keeps over-installing without a diagnostic.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "callSites": {
    "current": "registry-features.ts declares { name: 'slash', files: [slash.tsx], registryDependencies: ['@plate/inline-combobox'] }; deriveRegistryPackageDependencies sees slash.tsx import './inline-combobox', resolves its owner, and throws 'missing direct registry dependency' unless that edge is authored.",
    "proposed": "(proposed) registry-features.ts declares { name: 'slash', files: [slash.tsx] }; the analyzer adds registryDependencies ['@plate/inline-combobox'] from the import, while an item such as highlight keeps an authored '@plate/highlight-style' edge for CSS the source cannot express."
  },
  "previous": "2026-09-18-ui-menu-focus-and-block-insertion-ownership",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "reconciliation": [
    {
      "record": "2026-09-18-ui-menu-focus-and-block-insertion-ownership",
      "question": "What is the smallest copied composition contract that keeps kit membership, installation metadata and toolbar policy explicit?",
      "action": "supersedes",
      "reason": "Its focus and insertion target is adopted in live source; this review names the remaining installation-metadata gap instead."
    },
    {
      "record": "2026-09-18-slash-ui-actions-execution",
      "question": "What is the smallest copied composition contract that keeps kit membership, installation metadata and toolbar policy explicit?",
      "action": "retains",
      "reason": "Typed insert and upsert, item-scoped finalFocus and the transforms.ts deletion hold on the live tree; its proof receipt stays historical."
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    "Keeping validation-only registry edges loses. The checker already resolves the unique owner of every copied import and fails on ambiguity, so the authored edge repeats its answer, and an edge whose import was removed keeps over-installing silently.",
    "Deriving import-required registry edges in the same analyzer, keeping authored edges only for styles, bundles and companions, and failing only on ambiguous ownership is the lane to pursue. It deletes about 361 hand-maintained lines and leaves metadata that is pure install intent.",
    "Amending plate.md and plate-ui.mdc to bless hand-listed edges as an explicit install graph loses, because the generated metadata snapshot and public payloads already show the full graph.",
    "Stopping copied menus (slash, insert, block menu) from importing optional-feature descriptors, so their installs stop pulling the AI SDK, katex, excalidraw and mermaid peers, is rejected. plate.md:930 keeps integration with the item it modifies even with an optional dependency, and users trim copied items.",
    "Extending item-scoped finalFocus to the context-menu adapters to remove block-menu's last valueRef handshake is real but has one caller. It is a small adapter follow-up, not a direction change.",
    "A universal command catalog, a package menu-focus API or merged live and static kits stay rejected for the reasons in the 2026-09-18 record."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Source review plus one scratch census; nothing was built or installed. The census parses imports with a regex over the base provider's copied files and may misclassify type-only or re-exported edges; the checker's own parser is authoritative. Registry and adapter files are committed. docs/vision/plate.md has staged edits from another session that shift line numbers but not the cited law. No generated install, provider build or browser focus run was repeated, so the slash-ui-actions proof stays historical.",
